WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV — satiation (30s) Narrator Gabriel

1
00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:03.129
Once a bug is fixed or an invoice reconciles,

2
00:00:03.129 --> 00:00:06.828
throwing ten times more machine tokens at it adds nothing.

3
00:00:07.248 --> 00:00:11.200
Task Satiation defines the exact finish line of one job,

4
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:15.152
separating it cleanly from Jevons rebound in total jobs.

5
00:00:15.572 --> 00:00:19.132
API token prices can drop ninety percent a year,

6
00:00:19.132 --> 00:00:23.435
yet every new rebound workload still draws real megawatts.

7
00:00:23.855 --> 00:00:27.635
Smart systems stop spending the instant a task verifies,

8
00:00:27.635 --> 00:00:31.281
rather than burning unbounded compute past completion.
